      "body": "## Purpose\n\n`_fused_moe_lora_shrink` and `_fused_moe_lora_expand` build TMA descriptors with `triton.tools.tensor_descriptor.TensorDescriptor`, but nothing in vLLM imports `triton.tools.tensor_descriptor`. `import triton` does not load that submodule, so in a fresh process the first call that takes the TMA path fails:\n\n```\nAttributeError: module 'triton.tools' has no attribute 'tensor_descriptor'\n```\n\nOn main this path runs whenever `max_lora_rank > 128` (above the one-shot kernel's limit) on a GPU with TMA support. It usually goes unnoticed in tests because some earlier test in the same process has already imported the submodule.\n\nThis PR imports `TensorDescriptor` from `triton.tools.tensor_descriptor` where it is used.\n\nThis is the first of a stack that splits #64653:\n\n1. this PR: import fix\n2. #64653: use the shrink/expand kernels for batches of up to 64 tokens\n3. #64746: problem-sized default configs, threshold 256\n4. #64747: fp32 intermediate, single output rounding\n5. #64748: remove the small-batch kernel\n\n## Test Plan\n\nNew `test_fused_moe_lora_kernel_large_rank_fallback_fresh_process` runs one rank-256 case of `test_fused_moe_lora_kernel_large_rank_fallback` in a new interpreter (`spawn_new_process_for_each_test`).\n\n## Test Result\n\n- On main the new test fails with the `AttributeError` above (GB200 and H200). With this PR it passes.\n- `tests/lora/test_fused_moe_lora_kernel.py` on 1 GPU: 422 passed, 12 skipped (GB200 and H200).\n\nDiff: 2 files, +19 / -4.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
